 5V to 220V is a 44x boost. Your netlist used a 5.8u on-time in 10u period (58% duty). 5.8u/10u = 58% D, which is a 1.43x boost. Not a 44x boost. You must change the duty cycle to achieve a 44x boost, not a 1.43x boost. The gate pulse must be adjusted to get a high duty cycle (97.5% D) for a 44x boost. 4.5V to 220V is 44x boost. 220/4.5 = 48.89, so D should be 1 - 4.5/220 = 0.9773 (97.73% D). 97.73% D requires t_on = 9.77u, period = 10u. 10u period is 100kHz, which is reasonable for 5V to 220V boost. Rload = 220^2 / 250 = 193.6, which is correct. L1 in sw 100u is correct for 5V to 220V. M1 sw gate 0 0 NMOS is correct. D1 sw out DIODE is correct. C1 out 0 100u is correct. Vgate gate 0 PULSE(0 12 0 1n 1n 9.77u 10u) is the correct gate timing for 97.73% D. Your previous netlist used 5.8u/10u = 58% D, which was a 1.43x boost. You must change the gate pulse timing to 9.77u/10u = 97.73% D for a 44x boost. This will cause the circuit to work correctly and achieve the 220V output.
